{"id": "hrc-split-purchases", "title": "One $59,473 invoice, six purchase orders: how HRC beat the $10,000 cap", "seconds": 130.4, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "tempo": 1.018, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "4e2b75ddf231b3ba", "words": 411, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[9]"], "text": "San Francisco has a shortcut for small purchases. Under 10,000 dollars, a department can skip the contract and the bidding.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 6.22, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Prop Q", "sub": "small purchases, no contract, no bidding", "chip": "under $10,000"}, "emph": ["10,000 dollars"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.8, 0.95, 1.03, 1.46, 1.6, 1.82, 2.86, 3.12, 3.32, 3.64, 4.05, 4.13, 4.54, 4.67, 4.91, 5.02, 5.47, 5.57, 5.67]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The rule is called Prop Q, and you can’t split an order to stay under the cap.", "t0": 6.34, "t1": 9.71, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Prop Q", "sub": "one-off needs, like supplies", "chip": "no splitting"}, "emph": ["split"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.44, 0.68, 1.0, 1.51, 1.66, 1.75, 1.95, 2.18, 2.27, 2.51, 2.6, 2.76, 2.93, 3.02]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "So what happens when one bill is bigger than the cap? Here’s one. How big?", "t0": 9.83, "t1": 14.44, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "One bill", "sub": "bigger than the cap"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.4, 0.76, 0.93, 1.09, 1.31, 1.41, 1.64, 1.78, 1.87, 2.7, 3.0, 3.67, 3.87]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "59,473 dollars.", "t0": 14.44, "t1": 17.14, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$59,473.41", "label": "one arena invoice, July 2023"}, "emph": ["59,473"], "wt": [0.04, 0.57, 1.04, 1.28, 1.64, 2.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "status"], "text": "In 2025, the Controller, the City’s money watchdog, audited the Human Rights Commission, called HRC.", "t0": 17.66, "t1": 23.75, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Official findings", "sub": "Controller and City Attorney audit, Sep 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.33, 0.99, 1.12, 1.78, 1.93, 2.23, 2.47, 3.42, 3.9, 4.01, 4.28, 4.49, 5.19, 5.45]}, {"scene": "find1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "story[2]"], "text": "The first finding is that bill, from the Golden State Warriors’ arena. HRC cut it into pieces. How many?", "t0": 23.97, "t1": 30.28, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "One invoice", "sub": "$59,473.41"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Six purchase orders", "sub": "five of $10,000, one of $9,473.41"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "One voucher", "sub": "paid Sep 12, 2023"}], "kicker": "The first finding"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.35, 0.71, 0.81, 0.95, 1.52, 1.71, 1.81, 2.09, 2.32, 2.68, 3.59, 4.29, 4.47, 4.56, 4.73, 5.48, 5.67]}, {"scene": "find1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Six.", "t0": 30.28, "t1": 30.86, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "6", "label": "purchase orders for one invoice", "sub": "five of exactly $10,000, one for the rest"}, "emph": ["Six"], "wt": [0.04]}, {"scene": "find2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "The second finding is the big picture.", "t0": 31.48, "t1": 33.0, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Small purchases", "kicker": "The second finding", "sub": "July 2020 to September 2024", "chip": "$2,628,055 in Prop Q buys"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.7, 0.8, 0.9, 1.09]}, {"scene": "find2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "Over four years, HRC spent 2,628,055 dollars this way.", "t0": 33.12, "t1": 36.8, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Small purchases", "kicker": "The second finding", "sub": "July 2020 to September 2024", "chip": "$2,628,055 in Prop Q buys"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.5, 0.89, 1.58, 1.85, 2.05, 2.25, 2.5, 2.73, 2.98, 3.28, 3.43]}, {"scene": "find2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[0]"], "text": "How much got around the rules?", "t0": 36.92, "t1": 38.5, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Small purchases", "kicker": "The second finding", "sub": "July 2020 to September 2024", "chip": "$2,628,055 in Prop Q buys"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.38, 0.52, 0.71, 0.81]}, {"scene": "find2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[0]"], "text": "1.79 million dollars.", "t0": 38.5, "t1": 40.33, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.79 million", "label": "got around purchasing controls", "sub": "68 percent of its Prop Q spending"}, "emph": ["1.79"], "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.55, 0.86, 1.06, 1.34]}, {"scene": "find3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "story[3]"], "text": "The third finding: single payments, meant for refunds to people who aren’t City vendors.", "t0": 40.95, "t1": 45.05, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Single payments", "kicker": "The third finding", "sub": "meant for refunds and claims"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.35, 0.87, 1.21, 1.8, 2.01, 2.19, 2.68, 2.79, 3.05, 3.17, 3.37, 3.61]}, {"scene": "find3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "HRC sent 3,133,332 dollars this way. How many of those payments were the wrong way to pay?", "t0": 45.17, "t1": 51.25, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The right way to pay?", "kicker": "The third finding", "sub": "$3,133,332 in single payments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.62, 0.83, 1.05, 1.34, 1.61, 1.82, 2.1, 2.42, 2.6, 3.44, 3.61, 3.77, 3.83, 4.01, 4.38, 4.5, 4.59, 4.78, 4.89, 4.99]}, {"scene": "find3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["story[3]", "established[2]"], "text": "All 694.", "t0": 51.25, "t1": 52.61, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "694", "label": "single payments, every one ineligible", "sub": "$1.14 million of it just under $10,000"}, "emph": ["All"], "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.47, 0.74]}, {"scene": "find4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "The fourth finding is rent, paid for a person facing eviction.", "t0": 53.23, "t1": 56.25, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Rent for a tenant", "kicker": "The fourth finding", "sub": "Windsor Communities, June 27, 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.71, 0.85, 1.51, 1.77, 1.9, 1.96, 2.27, 2.58]}, {"scene": "find4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[3]"], "text": "But the landlord’s manager wouldn’t send a bill.", "t0": 56.37, "t1": 58.67, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["invoice one", "$9,393.37"], "b": ["invoice two", "$6,702.63"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.26, 0.74, 1.09, 1.32, 1.51, 1.56]}, {"scene": "find4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[3]"], "text": "So an HRC worker wrote two bills, at the director’s direction. Both under the cap.", "t0": 58.67, "t1": 63.49, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["invoice one", "$9,393.37"], "b": ["invoice two", "$6,702.63"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.23, 0.35, 0.91, 1.29, 1.54, 1.75, 2.24, 2.4, 2.5, 2.96, 3.8, 4.14, 4.34, 4.44]}, {"scene": "find4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "established[3]"], "text": "That breaks the record, because a bill should come from whoever gets paid. Another rent payment came with a falsified tax form.", "t0": 63.61, "t1": 69.51, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A falsified W-9", "kicker": "The fourth finding", "sub": "another rent payment, June 28, 2022"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.39, 0.5, 0.97, 1.25, 1.3, 1.51, 1.69, 1.87, 2.01, 2.33, 2.52, 3.57, 3.92, 4.11, 4.44, 4.62, 4.76, 4.83, 5.3, 5.6]}, {"scene": "find5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "A former adviser was paid in split payments, with no contract. How much, over eleven months?", "t0": 69.73, "t1": 74.86, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "A former senior policy adviser", "kicker": "More findings", "sub": "paid in split payments, no contract"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.38, 0.8, 0.93, 1.12, 1.2, 1.45, 1.87, 2.03, 2.19, 3.29, 3.49, 3.75, 3.97, 4.27]}, {"scene": "find5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[4]", "established[12]"], "text": "151,250 dollars.", "t0": 74.86, "t1": 78.44, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$151,250", "label": "over eleven months, no contract"}, "emph": ["151,250"], "wt": [0.04, 0.27, 0.55, 1.15, 2.07, 2.41, 2.72, 3.04]}, {"scene": "find5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[5]"], "text": "The audit’s total: of 6.3 million dollars paid outside contracts, 4.6 million broke the rules or likely did.", "t0": 78.96, "t1": 85.69, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paid outside contracts", "$6.3 million"], "b": ["ineligible or likely ineligible", "$4.6 million"]}, "emph": ["4.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.44, 1.2, 1.36, 1.58, 1.79, 1.99, 2.24, 2.56, 2.77, 3.11, 4.03, 4.29, 4.51, 4.74, 5.07, 5.34, 5.44, 5.89, 6.09, 6.41]}, {"scene": "find5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "established[10]", "established[11]"], "text": "Who was watching the money? HRC had no finance manager until December 2023.", "t0": 85.81, "t1": 90.35, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "No finance manager", "kicker": "Who was watching?", "sub": "until December 2023", "chip": "grant budget $12.0 million; ledger $71.7 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.56, 0.65, 1.48, 2.06, 2.21, 2.37, 2.74, 3.11, 3.34, 3.73, 3.97]}, {"scene": "find5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "established[10]", "established[11]"], "text": "In September 2024, its Prop Q buying was suspended.", "t0": 90.47, "t1": 93.62, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "No finance manager", "kicker": "Who was watching?", "sub": "until December 2023", "chip": "grant budget $12.0 million; ledger $71.7 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.76, 1.63, 1.8, 2.05, 2.26, 2.51, 2.62]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "One more piece is a pattern in City data, not an official finding.", "t0": 93.84, "t1": 97.03, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Orders just under the cap", "kicker": "A pattern, not a finding", "sub": "City purchase-order data"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.37, 0.68, 0.81, 0.87, 1.23, 1.35, 1.6, 2.18, 2.37, 2.45, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[6]"], "text": "Count the orders paid between 9,000 and 10,000 dollars.", "t0": 97.15, "t1": 99.9, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Orders just under the cap", "kicker": "A pattern, not a finding", "sub": "City purchase-order data"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.37, 0.66, 0.87, 1.17, 1.37, 1.68, 1.78, 1.95, 2.26]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[6]"], "text": "Fiscal 2019: 3. Then 17.", "t0": 100.02, "t1": 102.59, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Orders paid $9,000 to $10,000", "rows": [["FY2019", "3"], ["FY2022", "17"], ["FY2023", "25"], ["FY2024", "50"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.7, 1.28, 1.79, 2.02]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[6]"], "text": "Then 25. And in fiscal 2024?", "t0": 102.71, "t1": 105.33, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Orders paid $9,000 to $10,000", "rows": [["FY2019", "3"], ["FY2022", "17"], ["FY2023", "25"], ["FY2024", "50"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.96, 1.17, 1.28, 1.7, 1.97]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "established[6]"], "text": "50.", "t0": 105.33, "t1": 105.81, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "50", "label": "orders just under the cap, FY2024", "sub": "then 2 in FY2025"}, "emph": ["50"], "wt": [0.04]}, {"scene": "lead", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why"], "text": "Then 2, after the director left. Real needs spread out below a cap.", "t0": 106.33, "t1": 109.83, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A pile-up in the top tenth"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.48, 0.72, 0.82, 1.21, 1.95, 2.19, 2.41, 2.69, 2.85, 3.1, 3.17]}, {"scene": "charge", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[7]", "story[5]"], "text": "Prosecutors charged the former director, Sheryl Davis.", "t0": 110.05, "t1": 112.58, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Sheryl Davis", "kicker": "The charge", "sub": "former HRC director · The San Francisco Standard reported a not-guilty plea"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.59, 0.9, 1.0, 1.28, 1.72, 2.04]}, {"scene": "charge", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[7]", "story[5]"], "text": "Mission Local reported they put the misuse at about 350,000 dollars.", "t0": 112.7, "t1": 116.78, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["audit: broke the rules", "$4.6 million"], "b": ["charges, as Mission Local reported", "about $350,000"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.66, 1.03, 1.21, 1.4, 1.5, 1.96, 2.1, 2.33, 2.59, 2.87, 3.17, 3.53]}, {"scene": "charge", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[4]"], "text": "A charge is an allegation, not a conviction.", "t0": 116.9, "t1": 118.95, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A charge is an allegation, not a conviction."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.5, 0.6, 1.33, 1.51, 1.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "The audit doesn’t say the money was stolen. No vendor is blamed. And no money has been reported recovered.", "t0": 119.17, "t1": 124.03, "shot": "b30", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That the money was stolen", "That any vendor did wrong", "Any money recovered"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.35, 0.59, 0.73, 0.82, 1.01, 1.13, 1.89, 2.08, 2.35, 2.44, 3.29, 3.46, 3.6, 3.79, 3.9, 4.04, 4.42]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "The department accepted the audit. The criminal case is still open.", "t0": 124.15, "t1": 127.29, "shot": "b32", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.46, 0.85, 0.97, 1.72, 1.88, 2.18, 2.42, 2.51, 2.76]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.41, "t1": 129.51, "shot": "b33", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.63, 0.78, 1.04, 1.15, 1.24, 1.48, 1.73]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "find1": "Finding 1 · one bill, six orders", "find2": "Finding 2 · $1.79 million", "find3": "Finding 3 · single payments", "find4": "Finding 4 · invoices written inside", "find5": "More findings", "lead": "The pattern · 3 to 50", "charge": "The charge", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "document"}